#ROOM
Vnum     40601
Name     Bodhi Landing Pad~
Sector   field~
Flags    can_land~
Desc     Salt air and the distant sound of surf greet you here, on a
modest landing pad set into open grassland above Masara's southern
coast. Bodhi's low, colorful rooftops are visible in the near
distance, unlike the stark stonework of the Temples elsewhere on
Tython.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40602
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40941
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40602
Name     Coastal Path~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A well-worn path winds through tall grass here, the sea visible
and audible somewhere beyond the rise to the east. Bodhi's students
are known to wander this path for inspiration as much as exercise.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40601
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40603
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40603
Name     Gate of Bodhi~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Unlike the imposing gates elsewhere on Tython, Bodhi's entrance
is open and unguarded, framed by climbing vines and hand-painted
tilework. Visitors are welcomed here more freely than at any other
Temple.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40602
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40604
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40604
Name     Gallery Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Paintings, sculpture, and stranger works entirely fill this
bright, high-windowed hall, arranged with little apparent order
beyond what caught a curator's eye. Some pieces are centuries old;
others still smell faintly of fresh paint.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40603
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40607
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40605
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40606
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40602 1 40604
Reset O 0 40601 3 40604
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40605
Name     Music Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Instruments of every shape fill this warm, wood-paneled room,
some clearly ancient, others newly made. A half-remembered melody
seems to hang in the air even when no one is playing.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    40604
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 40602 3 40605
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40606
Name     Sculpture Garden~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     An open-air courtyard holds a scattering of sculptures here,
weathered by salt air and years alike. Some are recognizable figures;
others resist any single interpretation, which seems to be entirely
the point.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    40604
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40608
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40607
Name     Jake Fenn's Studio~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Half-finished works cover every surface of this cluttered
studio, in mediums ranging from paint to something that might be
sound made solid. Jake Fenn rarely finishes anything quickly, and
never apologizes for it.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    40604
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40601 1 40607
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     40608
Name     Amphitheater~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Tiered stone seating curves around a modest performance space
here, open to the sky and the sound of the nearby sea. Bodhi's
students perform here often, for audiences as small as a single
passing instructor.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    40606
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 40603 1 40608
#ENDROOM

#ENDAREA
